 )
+
+# Matches a 16-digit credit card number written as four groups of four digits.
+# The groups are either not separated at all, or all separated by one space, or
+# all separated by one hyphen; mixing separators is not valid. The three cases
+# are spelled out as alternatives rather than with a backreference to the
+# separator, since regexes are compiled to finite state machines for generation
+# and those do not support backreferences.
+credit_card = Regex(r"([0-9]{4}-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{4}|[0-9]{4} [0-9]{4} [0-9]{4} [0-9]{4}|[0-9]{16})")
